ionen \u00fcber unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. W\u00e4hlen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch k\u00f6nnen Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. W\u00e4hlen Notwendige Cookies sid Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 1 Stunde Enth\u00e4lt eine anonyme Nutzer-ID, um mehrere Anfragen eines Nutzers derselben HTTP-Session zuordnen zu k\u00f6nnen. cookieconsent_status Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Tage Dieses Cookie speichert Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen f\u00fcr diese Website. Webstatistik _pk_id* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 13 Monate Registriert eine eindeutige ID f\u00fcr einen Website-Besucher, die protokolliert, wie der Besucher die Website verwendet. Die Daten werden f\u00fcr Statistiken verwendet. _pk_ref* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at    Ablauf: 6 Monate Dieses Cookie wird als Referenz zur anonymen Tracking-Session auf der Seite eingesetzt. _pk_ses* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Minuten Dieses Cookie speichert eine eindeutige Session-ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: Dieses Session Cookie wird beim Schlie\u00dfen des Browsers wieder gel\u00f6scht Dieses Cookie speichert den Website-Besuch auf Basis einer Session- oder Visitor-ID. Anpassung speichern Abbrechen"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-tenure-track-qualification-agreement-eng-j2907.html": {"title": "Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, tenure track, qualification agreement Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-11 WU Vienna University of Economics and Business combines excellence with responsibility. Its rare triple accreditation by EQUIS, AACSB, and AMBA is a guarantee for the highest quality research and teaching in the fields of business, economics, and business law. WU\u2019s research is characterized by a wide diversity of disciplines practiced at WU, allowing researchers to deal with even the most complex research questions. International cooperation is very important to WU, and we encourage and support both faculty and student mobility. WU is also very aware of its responsibility to its students, faculty, and staff and is committed to gender equality, equal opportunities, accessibility, family-friendly working conditions, and sustainability. The Institute for Accounting and Auditing is looking for an Assistant Professor in Accounting Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting July 01, 2027, or soon thereafter, and limited for 6 years A qualification agreement will be concluded at the start of the employment (\u00a7 27 of the Collective Bargaining Agreement). Pursuant to WU\u2019s Personnel Development Plan, this position can only be fixed-term for up to six years. Once all objectives agreed upon in the qualification agreement have been fulfilled, the employment relationship can be made permanent. Employees who have successfully completed a qualification agreement are classified as associate professors. From an organizational regulation perspective they belong to the group of professors. Three years after successful completion of the qualification agreement, they are entitled to apply for promotion to full professor according to the By-Laws of WU \u00a7 43a. We are inviting applications for an Assistant Professor position (tenure track) in the field of financial accounting to join our institute. Members of the recruiting committee will attend the 2026 EAA Talent Workshop in Madrid and conduct interviews with prospective candidates. Candidates interested in this position are encouraged to attend the workshop and meet with us there. What to expect International faculty with a publication record in top tier accounting journals (e.g., The Accounting Review, Journal of Accounting Research, Journal of Accounting and Economics, Review of Accounting Studies). Strong international research network with regular guests from top-tier universities at our conferences and research seminars. Competitive compensation and strong research support, including research funding, data availability, and attractive teaching conditions. Tax incentive for eligible international researchers moving to Austria. Strong ties to business practice, professional associations, and policymakers. Highly motivated students with accounting majors in undergraduate, graduate, and PhD programs. What you have to offer We invite applications from researchers in the field of financial accounting. High-quality research using quantitative methods, with strong potential to publish in top-tier accounting journals. A completed PhD degree or anticipation to complete a PhD degree in the current academic year. Demonstrated active engagement with the international academic community, for example, through collaboration with international coauthors, research visits at other universities, or presentations at leading academic conferences. Candidates must have completed their PhD at a university other than WU or have at least two years of postdoctoral working experience at another university. It is an advantage if they demonstrate international academic experience\u2014such as a PhD from a non-Austrian university or postdoctoral work at a non-Austrian academic institution for at least two years. The ability to teach in English and commitment to excellence in teaching. Required submission materials: C.V. Cover letter Job market paper Research statement Teaching statement Three letters of reference Additional papers (optional) For further information about the position, please contact Professor Zolt\u00e1n Novotny-Farkas, at zoltan.novotny-farkas@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,980.80 (14 times per year). In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2907). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/2-Research-and-Teaching-Associates-eng-j2912.html": {"title": "2 Research and Teaching Associates", "description": "Job opportunity 2 Research and Teaching Associates at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! 2 Research and Teaching Associates Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-21 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 6 years The Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, as part of the Department of Management, is dedicated to studying human behaviour in organisations. You are interested in understanding how individuals can craft their jobs and make things happen in organisations, and/or how people can thrive and experience well-being at work, and pass on your findings to students in the classroom? You are also interested in understanding and helping organisations how to manage people in the context of emerging societal and technical developments, such as AI, changing workplace practices and preferences (e.g., WFH), political/economic uncertainty, and sustainability? This position opens doors to either an academic career or a later switch to a career in business. What to expect Research with Impact: The Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour focuses on timely issues related to positive behaviours in organisations. This means we examine how and when individuals will engage in positive behaviours and contribute to their organisation, as well as experience well-being and meaning in their work, particularly in the context of social and technological developments. You will make a valuable contribution to this research by supporting projects and academic publications. Writing a dissertation: You will conduct research within OB on a topic that is close to your heart, while spending a minimum of one third of your working time to writing your dissertation. Working in a team: At the Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, collaboration and mutual support are priorities. Together, we make a significant contribution to the advancement of our field. Building a lasting network: You will attend and co-organise international conferences and engage in dialogue with research partners and peers. Teaching students: You will plan and conduct courses in Organisational behaviour, for example in the existing SBWL programme of the institute (on the BSc level). You will also contribute to the administration of exams and evaluations. Advising students: You will be available to answer students\u2019 questions, provide feedback on seminar papers, and serve as a co-advisor for bachelor\u2019s theses. Performing organisational tasks: You will assist in the organisation of teaching, research and university life. What you have to offer Academic degree: You hold a diploma/master\u2019s degree in Business Administration, Management, or a related subject area, with a focus on Organisational Behaviour, or in Work & Organisational Psychology, that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU. Passion for research: You are motivated to delve into socially relevant research questions and publish your work in prestigious journals. Content expertise: You have solid knowledge in the area of organisational behaviour. Methodological skills: You have a solid knowledge of quantitative and/or qualitative research methods and the relevant software (such as Mplus, R, SPSS, or Stata, NVivo, or Atlas) for conducting empirical analyses. Language skills: You have excellent German and English skills and can express yourself very well in both languages, orally and in writing. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are capable of and willing to teach courses in German using multimedia formats. Personal qualities: You are curious, interested, and proactive. You can work independently but are also willing to contribute cooperatively as part of a team. Required submission materials (as one PDF file, in this order): Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV Transcripts of grade reports Contact information for 2\u20133 work and/or academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail) Additionally (as a separate PDF file): Full Master\u2019s/Diploma thesis If available: teaching evaluations If available: research paper We are looking forward to hearing from you! If you have any questions regarding the position or application documents, don\u2019t hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Uta Bindl at uta.bindl@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 21, 2026 (ID 2912). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2913.html": {"title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-10-21 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 3 years The Interdisciplinary Institute for Management and Organisational Behaviour, as part of the Department of Management, is dedicated to studying human behaviour in organisations. We particularly focus on research questions that relate to promoting positive behaviour in organisations and that enable individuals to reach their full potential and experience greater well-being at work. We also consider the contextual embeddedness of human behaviour at work, by studying the impact of emerging societal and technical developments and grand challenges, such as AI, changing workplace practices and preferences (e.g., WFH), political/economic uncertainty, and sustainability, on (positive) human behaviour in organisations. If these topics excite you, we look forward to receiving your application for the advertised position. What to expect Conduct research: You will actively contribute to the institute\u2019s research projects on organisational behaviour and further develop your own ideas. Teach and support courses: You will teach and support courses in OB, for example in the existing SBWL programme of the institute (on the BSc level) as well as in the Department of Management\u2019s Master programme. Supervise master\u2019s and bachelor\u2019s theses: You co-supervise master\u2019s and independently supervise bachelor\u2019s theses. Support organisation and administration: You will help fulfill the institute\u2019s administrative responsibilities. Work as part of a team: You will join a team of committed researchers who collaboratively advance research projects. Benefit from a strong research environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. What you have to offer Doctoral degree: You have successfully completed your doctoral degree in Business Administration, Management, or a related subject area, with a focus on Organisational Behaviour, or Work & Organisational Psychology, and demonstrate a strong commitment to research through promising publication projects. Peer-reviewed presentations at academic conferences and initial publications in journals listed on the WU Star Journal List or the Department of Management Journal List are an advantage. Passion for research: You are highly motivated to pursue an academic career and aim to publish your work in reputable scholarly journals. Relevant expertise and experience: You bring knowledge in areas that meaningfully connect with the focus of the Institute, such as investigating positive behaviours at work (e.g., motivation, proactivity/job crafting), or affect/well-being/meaningfulness in organisations. Ideally, you also have experience in studying human behaviour \u2018in context\u2019. Research methodology: You have in-depth training in quantitative methods including experience with common software tools (e.g., Mplus, R, Stata, SPSS) and/or qualitative research methods (e.g., grounded theory, thematic analysis). You have a clear understanding of the strengths and limitations of different methodological approaches. Ideally, you have some experience in using multi-method approaches in field research. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Teaching in German: You are also able and willing to teach courses in German. International experience and language skills: You can demonstrate international exposure in your studies. Strong English skills (both verbal and written) are mandatory. Digital skills: You are confident using standard software applications (e.g., Microsoft Office, video conferencing tools) and can quickly learn new systems. Engagement: You work independently, are organised, take initiative, and are excited to contribute as a team player. Required submission materials (as one PDF file, in this order): Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV Personal statement (briefly outlining research, teaching, and service activities; max 3 pages) Contact information for 2\u20133 academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail) Copies of 1\u20132 research papers If available: teaching evaluations Transcripts of grade reports Additionally (as a separate PDF file): Full PhD thesis We are looking forward to hearing from you! If you have any questions regarding the position or application documents, don\u2019t hesitate to contact Prof. Dr. Uta Bindl at uta.bindl@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 21,2026 (ID 2913). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2914.html": {"title": "Assistant professor, non-tenure track", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Nonprofit Management and Governance Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting March 1, 2027, or later (subject to negotiation), and ending after 2.5 years, no later than September 29, 2029. At the Institute for Nonprofit Management and Governance, we conduct research and teach on the governance and management of nonprofit organizations and social enterprises, on the civic engagement of citizens, and on the nonprofit sector as a whole. We share our findings with the scholarly community, with nonprofit practice, and with our students. The institute\u2019s research has appeared in leading journals in nonprofit studies, management, and sociology. The postdoctoral researcher will join the institute\u2019s work on the societal effects and embeddedness of nonprofit organizations. Current projects include research examining the relationship between nonprofits and their urban environments in cities worldwide, the social innovativeness of cities, and nascent work on the political backlash against nonprofit organizations. We are looking for a researcher who will contribute substantially to this line of work while developing an independent research agenda. What to expect Research: You will contribute actively to the institute\u2019s research projects on nonprofit organizations and their effects on society, and you will develop your own research agenda with the aim of publishing in leading international journals. Teaching: You will independently teach courses on organizations, the nonprofit sector, and social impact in Europe and beyond. Teaching is in English; teaching in German is welcome but not required. Thesis Supervision: You will give students feedback and help them develop their work, including co-supervising master\u2019s theses and independently supervising bachelor\u2019s theses. Organizational and Administrative Tasks: You will share in the institute\u2019s administrative responsibilities, including the organization of international research workshops on topics of mutual interest, and you will help prepare applications for collaborative grants. Collaborative Teamwork: You will join a team of researchers in nonprofit and organization studies who advance research projects together and who support you in developing your own projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. What you have to offer Academic Background: You have completed, or are close to completing, a doctoral degree in management, sociology, nonprofit and public management, urban planning, or a related field. The doctoral degree must be in hand at the start date of the contract. Research Record: You demonstrate a strong commitment to research through promising publication projects and experience in scientific research projects. Peer-reviewed conference presentations and initial publications in journals listed on the WU Star Journal List or the Department of Management Journal List (both accessible online) are an advantage. Subject Expertise: Your work addresses the societal effects of nonprofit organizations. Knowledge of nonprofit management and governance, social entrepreneurship and innovation, urban governance, or the civic dynamics of place-based communities is an advantage. Research Methods: You have a strong empirical research profile with experience in quantitative and qualitative analysis. We expect deep knowledge in one method, but experience with mixed methods and computational social science, including natural language processing, is welcome. Teaching: You are willing and prepared to teach in the areas of nonprofit management and social innovation. Prior experience teaching at the university level and familiarity with multimedia teaching and learning formats are an advantage. Language Skills: Strong English skills are essential. German is not required but is an advantage. Engagement: You work independently, take initiative, and act as a team player. You are willing to organize research events such as workshops and professional development sessions, and you take an active part in scholarly communities such as AoM, ISTR, ARNOVA, ASA, and SASE. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Want to join the WU? Please submit the following materials as a single PDF file, in this order: Cover letter, including your earliest possible and preferred start dates CV, indicating when you were or will be awarded your PhD Research statement (max. 2 pages) Teaching statement (max. 2 pages) and, if available, evidence of teaching excellence Contact information for two to three academic references (name, affiliation, e-mail); references will be contacted for shortlisted candidates One or two writing samples, ideally solo- or first-authored working papers or publications Please also submit your full PhD thesis as a separate PDF file. Application documents may be submitted in English or German through the WU online application tool (Reference number: [ID 2914]). Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis starting October 28, 2026, until the position is filled. For questions about the position or the application documents, please contact Prof. Christof Brandtner at christof.brandtner@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2914). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Fachkraft-Universitaetsbibliothek-Benutzungsmanagement-de-j2908.html": {"title": "Stellenangebot Fachkraft Universit\u00e4tsbibliothek (Benutzungsmanagement) bei think:impact", "description": "Stellenangebot Fachkraft Universit\u00e4tsbibliothek (Benutzungsmanagement) bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. Um Ihnen einen bestm\u00f6glichen Service zu bieten und die Verwendung mancher Funktionen zu erleichtern, verwenden wir Cookies. Mit der Nutzung dieser Seite erkl\u00e4ren Sie sich mit der Verwendung von Cookies einverstanden. Die Einwilligung kann jeder Zeit mit Wirkung f\u00fcr die Zukunft widerrufen werden. Mehr Informationen dar\u00fcber, welche Daten gespeichert werden, erhalten Sie hier. . Ja, ich bin einverstanden Cookies anpassen Ablehnen DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zur\u00fcck Jetzt bewerben! Fachkraft Universit\u00e4tsbibliothek (Benutzungsmanagement) Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4t Wien B\u00fcro, Verwaltung, Sachbearbeitung Vollzeit Publizierung bis: 21.10.2026 Sie wollen mit Ihrer Arbeit etwas bewegen, Verantwortung \u00fcbernehmen und so die Rahmenbedingungen f\u00fcr Spitzenforschung und -lehre schaffen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten k\u00f6nnen. An einer der gr\u00f6\u00dften und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4ten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualit\u00e4t auch Lebensqualit\u00e4t ist. Wir suchen Verst\u00e4rkung in der Universit\u00e4tsbibliothek Vollzeit, 40 Stunden/Woche Ab 02.11.2026 Sie wollen kommunikativer Mittelpunkt des Bibliothekszentrums sein? Mit unserem Team die WU-Studierenden, Mitarbeitenden und andere Bibliotheksnutzer*innen bei der Mediennutzung unterst\u00fctzen? In dieser Funktion innerhalb der Abteilung Benutzungsmanagement servicieren und beraten Sie alle Bibliotheksnutzer*innen bez. Entlehnung und Benutzung. Was Sie erwartet Bibliotheksnutzer*innen servicieren und betreuen: Sie machen Servicedienst am Bibliotheksempfang und stellen Bibliotheksausweise aus. Sie sind erste Ansprechpartner*in der Bibliothek und erteilen Ausk\u00fcnfte rund um Entlehnung und Benutzung Medienentlehnung: Sie f\u00fchren Entlehnungen im Bibliothekssystem Alma durch Printmedien betreuen: Sie adjustieren Medien, stellen sie ins Regal und heben sie aus. Sie bereiten Medien f\u00fcr den/die Buchbinder*in vor Datenmanagement im Bibliothekssystem Alma: Sie k\u00fcmmern sich um die Datenpflege und halten Benutzer*innen- und Exemplardaten aktuell Im Team arbeiten: Im Benutzungsmanagement erwartet Sie ein Team von 12 Personen, mit denen Sie gemeinsam die Entlehnung und Benutzung koordinieren Dienste zur Abdeckung von \u00d6ffnungszeiten und Samstagdienst: Sie \u00fcbernehmen im Anlassfall auch Servicedienste von Kolleg*innen und versehen Dienst an einigen Samstagen Was Sie mitbringen Einschl\u00e4gige Ausbildung/Berufserfahrung: Sie haben die Lehre zur/zum Bibliotheksassistent*in abgeschlossen oder haben Berufspraxis im Bibliotheksbereich oder einem vergleichbaren Umfeld Ausgepr\u00e4gte Dienstleistungsorientierung: Sie pflegen einen freundlichen, kompetenten und serviceorientierten Umgang mit allen Bibliotheksnutzer*innen Selbst\u00e4ndig, teamf\u00e4hig und sicheres Auftreten: Sie sind eigeninitiativ, haben ein sicheres Auftreten, erkennen, wo man anpacken muss und haben gleichzeitig Freude an der Zusammenarbeit mit unterschiedlichsten Charakteren Sprachkompetenz: Sie haben gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift, weitere Sprachen sind willkommen Zahlenaffin: So gut, wie Sie mit Worten umgehen k\u00f6nnen, schaffen Sie das auch im Umgang mit Zahlen IT-Anwendungskenntnisse: Sie sind sicher im Umgang mit IT-Systemen wie z.B. MS Office Verl\u00e4sslichkeit und Genauigkeit: Sie sind bei s\u00e4mtlichen Aufgaben verl\u00e4sslich und genau Was wir Ihnen bieten 6 Wochen Urlaub/Erholungszeit Flexible Arbeitszeiten im Rahmen der Gleitzeit Vielf\u00e4ltiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt \u00fcber Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielf\u00e4ltigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit \u00fcber 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute \u00f6ffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr dar\u00fcber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt betr\u00e4gt 2.581,20 Euro brutto. T\u00e4tigkeitsbezogene Vordienstzeiten k\u00f6nnen zu einem h\u00f6heren Einstiegsgehalt f\u00fchren. Dar\u00fcber hinaus bieten wir eine Vielzahl an attraktiven Sozialleistungen an. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis sp\u00e4testens 21.10.2026 (Kennzahl: 2908). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Die WU sch\u00e4tzt Diversit\u00e4t und Inklusion und bem\u00fcht sich aktiv um ein vielf\u00e4ltiges Team. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterst\u00fctzt. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Cookieeinstellungen Close Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind f\u00fcr die Funktionalit\u00e4t unserer Website erforderlich\nund k\u00f6nnen in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgew\u00e4hlt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen \u00fcber unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. W\u00e4hlen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch k\u00f6nnen Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. W\u00e4hlen Notwendige Cookies sid Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 1 Stunde Enth\u00e4lt eine anonyme Nutzer-ID, um mehrere Anfragen eines Nutzers derselben HTTP-Session zuordnen zu k\u00f6nnen. cookieconsent_status Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Tage Dieses Cookie speichert Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen f\u00fcr diese Website. Webstatistik _pk_id* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 13 Monate Registriert eine eindeutige ID f\u00fcr einen Website-Besucher, die protokolliert, wie der Besucher die Website verwendet. Die Daten werden f\u00fcr Statistiken verwendet. _pk_ref* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at    Ablauf: 6 Monate Dieses Cookie wird als Referenz zur anonymen Tracking-Session auf der Seite eingesetzt. _pk_ses* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Minuten Dieses Cookie speichert eine eindeutige Session-ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: Dieses Session Cookie wird beim Schlie\u00dfen des Browsers wieder gel\u00f6scht Dieses Cookie speichert den Website-Besuch auf Basis einer Session- oder Visitor-ID. Anpassung speichern Abbrechen"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2910.html": {"title": "Research and Teaching Associate", "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-14 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institut f\u00fcr Retailing & Data Science Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting as soon as possible and ending after 6 years The Institute for Retailing & Data Science (RDS) works at the intersection of quantitative marketing, machine learning, and causal inference. We study how digital markets work - from grocery retailing to music streaming. Through long-standing partnerships, we have access to large-scale, real-world datasets from major retailers and online platforms, including transaction-level retail data, streaming-data from the music industry, and data we collect ourselves at scale via APIs and automated data collection. Our research combines modern data science methods - machine learning, deep learning, and causal ML - with state-of-the-art econometric approaches, such as quasi-experimental designs (e.g., modern difference-in-differences estimators), to answer questions that matter to managers, platforms, and policymakers. We publish in leading international journals, present at top conferences in marketing, economics, and machine learning, and actively share our findings with the broader public. In teaching, we prepare the next generation of marketing professionals to shape the digital transformation of the retail sector. You will join a vibrant, internationally oriented team with a strong collaborative culture, close ties across WU, and an active international research network. What to expect Writing a dissertation (one third of your working hours): You will develop your own research agenda within one of our active research streams, working with real market data from day one. Current research streams include: AI-generated content in markets for information goods: Generative AI is rapidly transforming markets such as music streaming. Dissertation topics include detecting AI-generated content and streaming fraud, estimating the impact of AI content on demand, revenues, and creators, and evaluating policy interventions such as AI-content labels. Retail and platform analytics: Demand modeling, shopping basket analysis, pricing and promotion analytics, personalized recommendations, and channel management; using transaction data from major retail partners. Causal inference and machine learning: Estimating causal effects in large-scale market data, using approaches ranging from modern difference-in-differences designs to double/debiased machine learning and heterogeneous treatment effect estimation - with applications to demand estimation, media exposure, pricing, and promotions. Bilateral AI - combining sub-symbolic and symbolic methods: Integrating deep learning with symbolic reasoning and causal knowledge (causal representation learning) to build models that are both predictive and interpretable. Data & infrastructure: You will work with large, proprietary, real-world datasets (e.g., from major retailers and online platforms) and modern tooling for large-scale data processing. Conferences & network: You will present your work at leading international conferences and collaborate within our international academic network. Teaching & co-supervision: The regular teaching load is approx. one course per term; you will also co-supervise bachelor's and master's theses. Organizational tasks: As part of the team, you will support selected organizational tasks of the institute. What you have to offer We are looking for a candidate who meets the following criteria: You hold a diploma or master's degree with strong academic performance in business, economics, computer science, data science, statistics, or a related quantitative field that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU. You have a strong quantitative mindset and genuine enthusiasm for empirical research - you enjoy working with large-scale, real-world data and turning it into credible evidence. You are proficient in at least one statistical programming language (e.g., Python, or R) and eager to deepen your technical skills as part of your doctoral training. You are interested in the methods we use across the full research pipeline - automated data collection (e.g., web scraping, APIs), large-scale data processing (e.g., SQL databases), machine learning and deep learning (e.g., gradient boosting, PyTorch), and causal inference (e.g., quasi-experimental designs, double/debiased ML). You bring experience in or curiosity about our substantive domains (retailing and digital platforms), such as demand modeling, pricing and promotion analytics, recommender systems, channel management, or the economics of AI-generated content. You have an excellent command of written and spoken English ; German language skills are an asset. Since the position includes teaching responsibilities, prior teaching or instructional-support experience (e.g., tutoring, grading, course assistance) is appreciated. You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 14, 2026 (ID 2910). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2920.html": {"title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Digital Marketing and Behavioral Science Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting as soon as possible, and ending after 1 year Qualified candidates with disabilities are especially encouraged to apply for this position. If necessary, a reduction of the extent of employment is possible. We are offering a one-year Postdoctoral Researcher position in Marketing at the Chair of Digital Marketing & Behavioral Science (start date flexible, February 2027 the latest). The position is particularly suited for an early-career researcher who has completed or is close to completing their PhD and wants to use an intensive research-focused year to strengthen their academic profile, advance their publication pipeline, develop new research collaborations, and prepare for the international academic job market. As an interdisciplinary research group, we study consumer phenomena at the intersection of digital technologies, marketing, and behavioral science. Our research examines how developments such as artificial intelligence (AI), algorithms, digital platforms, and social media shape consumer behavior, purchase decisions, social interactions, and moral decision-making. Methodologically, we employ approaches ranging from behavioral lab and field experiments to quantitative analyses of large-scale secondary data and machine-learning methods. The WU Marketing Department offers a highly international and research-oriented environment with a strong track record in leading marketing journals. As a postdoctoral researcher, you will have the opportunity to pursue and further develop your own research agenda, while initiating new projects and collaborations with researchers at WU and within our international network. You will have access to funding for data collection, a dedicated conference travel budget, and international research and training opportunities. You will also be closely connected to WU\u2019s interdisciplinary research ecosystem around AI, technology, and society, including the Applied AI Competence Center and the Digital Humanism Center. What to expect Independent research: You will pursue and further develop your own research agenda, advance existing projects toward publication, and initiate new research projects and collaborations. You will be encouraged to target leading international journals in marketing and related fields. Strengthening your academic profile: The one-year position is designed to provide an intensive research environment in which you can strengthen your publication pipeline, sharpen your research profile, expand your academic network, and prepare for the next stage of an international academic career. Research collaboration: You will have opportunities to develop joint research projects with faculty at the Chair and the wider WU Marketing Department as well as with researchers in our international network. Depending on mutual research interests, these collaborations may include behavioral, field, quantitative, or computational research. Resources for your research: You will have access to funding opportunities for data collection and experiments, a dedicated conference travel budget, and international research and training opportunities. A strong research environment: You will become part of WU\u2019s highly research-oriented Marketing Department and participate in its research seminars, workshops, and academic exchange. You will also be connected to WU\u2019s broader interdisciplinary research ecosystem around AI, technology, and society , including the Applied AI Competence Center and the Digital Humanism Center. Building your international network: You will participate in international conferences and have opportunities to connect with researchers at leading international universities as well as industry partners. Teaching: You will plan and teach two courses per semester in WU\u2019s marketing programs and/or interdisciplinary programs related to the digital economy. Student supervision and mentoring: You will (co-)supervise Bachelor\u2019s and Master\u2019s theses, support selected student projects, including projects with industry partners, and contribute to the research development of junior researchers at the institute. Research, teaching, and organizational support: You will contribute to selected administrative and organizational activities related to research, teaching, and academic self-governance. What you have to offer PhD degree: You have completed, or are close to completing, a PhD in a field relevant to the position, such as marketing, consumer behavior, behavioral economics, psychology/social psychology, information systems, data science, quantitative marketing, or a related discipline. Strong research profile: You have an excellent academic record and a clearly identifiable research profile in an area related to digital marketing, consumer behavior, behavioral science, AI and technology, social media and digital platforms, or related topics. Research methods: You have strong methodological expertise in at least one of our main methodological areas: 1. Behavioral and experimental research , including lab, online, and/or field experiments; or 2. Quantitative and computational research , including secondary-data analysis, econometrics/causal inference, programming, computational methods, and/or machine learning. Publication potential: You have a strong research pipeline, including an academic research paper (\u201cjob market paper\u201d) that demonstrates the potential to publish in a leading international journal in marketing or a related field. Publications or papers under review at leading journals are an advantage. Independent research: You demonstrate the ability to develop theoretically and methodologically rigorous research questions and to independently move research projects from idea development through data collection and analysis to publication. International academic orientation: You are actively engaged in, or motivated to become further involved in, the international academic community through research collaborations and presentations at leading academic conferences. Interest in digital technologies and AI: You are intellectually curious about emerging digital technologies and their implications for consumers, organizations, and society and are open to incorporating AI and new computational tools into your research process where appropriate. Prior expertise in AI is welcome but not required. Teaching: You have demonstrated experience with and commitment to high-quality university teaching and are open to using innovative and digital teaching formats. Working style and collaboration: You combine intellectual curiosity and strong analytical skills with initiative and independence. You enjoy developing new research ideas and collaborating in an interdisciplinary and international research environment. Language skills: You have excellent written and spoken English skills. Knowledge of German is not required; German language skills are considered an advantage. Application: Applicants are required to upload a CV, cover letter, a job market paper, a research statement, a teaching statement including a list of courses taught and available teaching evaluations, and additional research papers (optional). The research statement should briefly outline the applicant\u2019s current research agenda and publication pipeline, as well as the research projects and goals they would like to pursue during the one-year postdoctoral position, including potential opportunities for collaboration. For further information about the position, please contact Christina Schamp at christina.schamp@wu.ac.at What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2920). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Organisationsentwicklerin-de-j2918.html": {"title": "Stellenangebot Organisationsentwickler*in bei think:impact", "description": "Stellenangebot Organisationsentwickler*in bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. Um Ihnen einen bestm\u00f6glichen Service zu bieten und die Verwendung mancher Funktionen zu erleichtern, verwenden wir Cookies. Mit der Nutzung dieser Seite erkl\u00e4ren Sie sich mit der Verwendung von Cookies einverstanden. Die Einwilligung kann jeder Zeit mit Wirkung f\u00fcr die Zukunft widerrufen werden. Mehr Informationen dar\u00fcber, welche Daten gespeichert werden, erhalten Sie hier. . Ja, ich bin einverstanden Cookies anpassen Ablehnen DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zur\u00fcck Jetzt bewerben! Organisationsentwickler*in Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4t Wien B\u00fcro, Verwaltung, Sachbearbeitung Voll/Teilzeit Publizierung bis: 04.11.2026 Sie wollen mit Ihrer Arbeit etwas bewegen, Verantwortung \u00fcbernehmen und so die Rahmenbedingungen f\u00fcr Spitzenforschung und -lehre schaffen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten k\u00f6nnen. An einer der gr\u00f6\u00dften und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4ten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualit\u00e4t auch Lebensqualit\u00e4t ist. Wir suchen Verst\u00e4rkung in der Abteilung Organizational and Talent Development Voll/Teilzeit, 32-40 Stunden/Woche Ab 11.01.2027 Sie lieben es, in einer Organisation gemeinsam mit Kolleg*innen Entwicklung und Ver\u00e4nderung voranzutreiben? Sie wollen Gro\u00dfes bewegen \u2013 und Rahmenbedingungen f\u00fcr Spitzenforschung und Lehre zu schaffen, trifft genau Ihr Interesse? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten und einen Mehrwert schaffen k\u00f6nnen. Sie sind Teil einer der gr\u00f6\u00dften und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4ten Europas und arbeiten auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualit\u00e4t auch Lebensqualit\u00e4t ist. Wir suchen Verst\u00e4rkung f\u00fcr die organisationale Weiterentwicklung unserer Universit\u00e4t. Was Sie erwartet Strategische Projekte begleiten: Sie begleiten strategische Projekte in unterschiedlichen organisatorischen Einheiten und \u00fcbernehmen die Verantwortung f\u00fcr die Gestaltung und Steuerung der damit verbundenen Prozesse. F\u00fchrungskr\u00e4fte und Projektverantwortliche beraten: Als Sparring-Partner*in und Berater*in unterst\u00fctzen Sie unsere F\u00fchrungskr\u00e4fte, Projektmanager*innen und Prozessverantwortlichen bei der Entwicklung passgenauer L\u00f6sungen, die langfristig Wirkung entfalten, wie beispielsweise Prozessoptimierungen. Organisation weiterentwickeln: Gemeinsam mit Kolleg*innen und Stakeholdern analysieren Sie \u00fcbergreifende Zusammenh\u00e4nge, identifizieren Potenziale und entwickeln Ma\u00dfnahmen zur Weiterentwicklung der Organisation. Strategische OE-Prozesse begleiten: Sie arbeiten an der Planung, Konzeptionierung und Begleitung von strategischen OE-Prozessen auf gesamtuniversit\u00e4rer Ebene mit. Workshops konzipieren und moderieren: Sie konzipieren und moderieren Workshops, die eine zielgerichtete Umsetzung von Entwicklungsprozessen unterst\u00fctzen. Was Sie mitbringen Abgeschlossenes Hochschulstudium und OE-Expertise: Abgeschlossenes Hochschulstudium sowie profunde Kenntnisse in der Organisationsentwicklung Berufserfahrung: Fundierte Berufserfahrung in vergleichbarer Position Beratungskompetenz: F\u00e4higkeit und Freude daran, Menschen und Organisationseinheiten mit unterschiedlichen Perspektiven und Anforderungen in gemeinsamen Vorhaben zu begleiten Hohe Serviceorientierung und ausgepr\u00e4gte soziale Kompetenz Kommunikative F\u00e4higkeiten und strategisches, analytisches Denken Selbstst\u00e4ndige, strukturierte und proaktive Arbeitsweise Sehr gute MS-Office-Kenntnisse und ausgepr\u00e4gte Affinit\u00e4t f\u00fcr Digitalisierung Ausgezeichnete Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse Was wir Ihnen bieten 6 Wochen Urlaub/Erholungszeit Flexible Arbeitszeiten im Rahmen der Gleitzeit Mobiles Arbeiten Vielf\u00e4ltiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt \u00fcber Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielf\u00e4ltigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit \u00fcber 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute \u00f6ffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr dar\u00fcber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt betr\u00e4gt 3.185,00 Euro brutto. Je nach Qualifikation und Erfahrung bieten wir eine \u00dcberzahlung in Kombination mit attraktiven Sozialleistungen. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis sp\u00e4testens 04.11.2026 (Kennzahl: 2918). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Die WU sch\u00e4tzt Diversit\u00e4t und Inklusion und bem\u00fcht sich aktiv um ein vielf\u00e4ltiges Team. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterst\u00fctzt. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Cookieeinstellungen Close Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind f\u00fcr die Funktionalit\u00e4t unserer Website erforderlich\nund k\u00f6nnen in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgew\u00e4hlt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen \u00fcber unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. W\u00e4hlen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch k\u00f6nnen Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. W\u00e4hlen Notwendige Cookies sid Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 1 Stunde Enth\u00e4lt eine anonyme Nutzer-ID, um mehrere Anfragen eines Nutzers derselben HTTP-Session zuordnen zu k\u00f6nnen. cookieconsent_status Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Tage Dieses Cookie speichert Ihre Cookie-Einstellungen f\u00fcr diese Website. Webstatistik _pk_id* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 13 Monate Registriert eine eindeutige ID f\u00fcr einen Website-Besucher, die protokolliert, wie der Besucher die Website verwendet. Die Daten werden f\u00fcr Statistiken verwendet. _pk_ref* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at    Ablauf: 6 Monate Dieses Cookie wird als Referenz zur anonymen Tracking-Session auf der Seite eingesetzt. _pk_ses* Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: 30 Minuten Dieses Cookie speichert eine eindeutige Session-ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domainname: jobs.wu.ac.at Ablauf: Dieses Session Cookie wird beim Schlie\u00dfen des Browsers wieder gel\u00f6scht Dieses Cookie speichert den Website-Besuch auf Basis einer Session- oder Visitor-ID. Anpassung speichern Abbrechen"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Project-staff-member-post-doc-eng-j2922.html": {"title": "Job opportunity Project staff member (post-doc)", "description": "Job opportunity Project staff member (post-doc) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Project staff member (post-doc) Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Ecological Economics Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 14 months (potential extension based on performance) Be part of an international research team contributing to shape the future of climate and nature finance within the international financial architecture. Work with top scholars to develop models for policy and financial impact. We are looking for a post-doctoral researcher in climate and nature finance, with a focus and interest on their international development aspects. The position is based at the Institute for Ecological Economics, within the Vienna University of Economics and Business, under the supervision of Irene Monasterolo. You will work with the experts of the Task Force on Climate, Development and the International Financial Architecture led by Boston University in collaboration with the G24 and V20 on reshaping international climate finance for development, in dialogue with multinational development banks and financial institutions. Within the project, you will contribute to inform how different financial arrangements and instruments could contribute to build resilience to climate and nature risks, in an inclusive and financial stability-aware way. You will explore the conditions for climate development finance to act a global shock absorber in the context of climate and nature risks. In particular, you will provide new conceptual and quantitative insights on debt, financial instruments and measures (e.g. Resilience and Sustainability Facility, Recovery and Resilience Facility, Capital Flow Management Measures, Regional Financing Arrangements, equity), including a global insurance scheme, for emerging markets and low-income economies (EMDEs). This is a crucial topic for the future of international development: growing socio-economic losses from climate change and ecosystem depletion, and geopolitical instability, contribute to decrease countries\u2019 fiscal space and to increase the cost of investing in resilience. In this context, EMDEs face a future of sluggish development, insufficient resilience and sustainability, and new debt crises, with cascading effects on the economy of Global North countries. You will work in close contact with a team of experts in climate finance for development with long experience in development finance institutions. You will have the opportunity to attend international research and policy workshops, conferences, and have policy impact, shaping the discussion about the international climate finance agenda. What to expect Developing quantitative tools (in particular Stock-Flow Consistent behavioral model and stress test models) for macro-financial risk assessment of climate and nature risks, and financial instruments. Collaborating with top scholars from leading institutions and think tanks (e.g., Boston University, Utrecht University, University of Venice, Bruegel) and engaging with the Task Force team. Driving impact by informing the design of financial instruments and financial policy in EMDEs. Contributing to academic output through publishing high-quality research in peer reviewed high ranked journals. Support the project dissemination activities by participating in relevant conferences, workshops, and seminars. What you have to offer We are looking for a motivated post-doctoral researcher with the following qualifications: PhD in Economics, Finance, Statistics, Physics, or a related field. Proven experience with macro-financial and financial risk modeling, using either Stock-Flow Consistent models, or Agent-Based models, or network models. Expertise and interest with climate and nature finance, and development finance. Strong coding skills in Matlab and Python. Fluency in English both spoken and written (other languages are a plus) and willingness to travel international for conferences and meetings. Ability to deliver quality and relevant work, meet deadlines, manage tasks independently, work in team. Ability to write and present research for academic and policy audiences independently. Location: Vienna, one of the cities with the highest quality of life in Europe, with access to facilities and a dynamic international research environment. Remuneration: in accordance with the applicable collective labour agreement, including social security coverage and paid annual leave. To apply, please send your curriculum vitae, including a letter of motivation and at least two published or unpublished papers. A first round of online interviews will take place at the beginning of November. Expected starting date of the position is December 2026. For more information about this position, please contact Prof. Dr. Irene Monasterolo ( irene.monasterolo@wu.ac.at ). What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac3,760.73 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2922). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2917.html": {"title": "Research and Teaching Associate", "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-21 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Digital Marketing and Behavioral Science Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting as soon as possible, and ending after 6 years Qualified candidates with disabilities are especially encouraged to apply for this position. If necessary, a reduction of the extent of employment is possible. We are offering a PhD position in Marketing at the Chair of Digital Marketing & Behavioral Science , with a flexible starting date (as early as possible). As an interdisciplinary research group, we study consumer phenomena at the intersection of digital technologies, marketing, and behavioral science. Our research examines how developments such as artificial intelligence (AI), algorithms, digital platforms, and social media shape consumer behavior, purchase decisions, social interactions, and moral decision-making. Methodologically, we employ a broad range of approaches, ranging from behavioral lab and field experiments to quantitative analyses of large-scale secondary data and machine-learning methods. The WU Marketing Department offers a highly international and research-oriented environment in which you will have the freedom to develop your own research agenda. You will have access to funding for data collection, a dedicated conference travel budget, and international doctoral courses and training opportunities , as well as a strong network of international research collaborators and industry partners. Beyond the Marketing Department, you will benefit from WU\u2019s growing interdisciplinary research ecosystem around technology and society, including the Applied AI Competence Center and the Digital Humanism Center , which brings together researchers interested in how digital technologies can be developed and used to serve people and society. What to expect Writing a dissertation: You will investigate your own research topic and spend one third of your working hours on your dissertation, with the goal of completing a PhD in Marketing and publishing your research in leading international journals. Key areas of research: Depending on your interests and methodological background, your research will primarily focus on one of two areas: Behavioral and experimental research: investigating consumer behavior in digital environments using lab, online, and field experiments. Quantitative and computational research: investigating marketing and consumer phenomena using secondary data, causal inference, computational methods, and/or machine-learning approaches. Across both areas, potential research topics include digital consumer behavior, artificial intelligence and human\u2013AI interaction, social media and digital platforms, algorithms and personalization, and the societal and ethical implications of digital technologies. Developing your own research agenda: You will have the freedom to develop your own research ideas within the broader research areas of the chair and collaborate on projects with faculty members and international research partners. Resources for your research: You will have access to funding for data collection and experiments, a dedicated conference travel budget, and international doctoral courses and training opportunities. An interdisciplinary research environment: You will be closely connected to WU\u2019s interdisciplinary research ecosystem around AI, technology, and society , including the Applied AI Competence Center and the Digital Humanism Center , and benefit from exchange with researchers from different disciplines working on the opportunities and implications of emerging technologies. Building up a personal network: You will participate in international conferences and connect with researchers from leading international universities as well as industry partners, including established companies, digital start-ups, and consulting firms. Doctoral courses: You will complete doctoral courses and participate in research seminars and workshops to further develop your theoretical and methodological expertise. Teaching: Starting after the second semester of your employment, you will typically teach one course per semester and gain experience in university-level teaching. Co-supervising Bachelor\u2019s and Master\u2019s theses: You will co-supervise Bachelor\u2019s and Master\u2019s theses and support selected student projects, including projects conducted in cooperation with industry partners. Research and teaching support: You will contribute to selected organizational and administrative activities related to research, teaching, and academic self-governance. What you have to offer Academic degree: You have a Master\u2019s degree (or expect to complete it before the agreed starting date) that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU, as well as a strong academic record. We particularly welcome applicants with a background related to one of the following areas: 1. Quantitative and computational fields: quantitative marketing, empirical methods, information systems, data science/big data analytics, machine learning, computer science, econometrics, or related fields. 2. Behavioral fields: marketing management, consumer behavior, behavioral economics, psychology/social psychology, or related fields. Interest in academic research: You have a strong interest in pursuing a PhD and conducting rigorous, internationally oriented research with the ambition to publish in leading academic journals in marketing and related fields. Experience with empirical research methods: You have initial experience with empirical research methods relevant to your background, such as experimental research, quantitative data analysis, econometrics, programming, computational methods, or machine learning. You do not need to cover the full range of methods, but should be interested in further developing your methodological skills during your PhD. Interest in digital technologies and AI: You are curious about emerging digital technologies and their implications for consumers, organizations, and society. You are open to developing new methodological and technological skills, including the use of AI and computational tools in the research process. Prior expertise in AI is welcome but not required. Willingness to use innovative teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia and digital teaching methods and to engage with innovative learning formats. Working style and collaboration: You have strong analytical and presentation skills, work independently and reliably, show initiative and intellectual curiosity, and enjoy developing ideas and collaborating in an interdisciplinary and international research environment. Language skills: You have excellent written and spoken English skills. Knowledge of German is not required; German language skills are considered an advantage. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 21, 2026 (ID 2917). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2919.html": {"title": "Research and Teaching Associate", "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business IT Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-21 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Digital Ecosystems Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting October 17, 2026, and ending after 3 years You want to work in a dynamic, open-minded and highly motivated team? Expect exciting research projects with a focus on Behavioral Decision Making, Digital Ecosystems, Digital Humanism, Data Science and AI, Decision Support, and Online Consumer Behavior. What to expect Research life: Collaborate with your colleagues on ongoing research projects at the Institute. Support Institute research projects and set up your own projects with a focus on topics in Behavioral Decision Making, Digital Ecosystems, Digital Humanism, Data Science and AI, Decision Support, and Online Consumer Behavior Teaching: Plan, create and teach courses. Advise students and co-supervise their theses and exams Build a personal network: Use the pre-doc phase to start building your personal network with contacts in research, industry and business. Opportunities to visit international partners in the Institute network. Organizational and administrative support: Support workshop and conference organization and work together with the Institute team on general tasks Writing a dissertation: You will be investigating your research topic and spending a third of your working hours on writing your dissertation. Interdisciplinary research is encouraged. Exciting research projects on digital ecosystems in a variety of contexts (e.g., financial, consumer, workplace) from a variety of perspectives (e.g., de-biasing and nudging, algorithm development, interface development, adaptive systems design, biosignal processing) with a variety of research methods (e.g., experiments, design science) Small team with intensive research mentoring Participation in international conferences (e.g., ICIS, ECIS, HICSS) Publication of research projects in international journals What you have to offer Academic degree: You have completed a master's degree that qualifies you for enrolling in a PhD program, preferably in one of the following subject areas:- Information Systems, Business Informatics- Information Technology, Software Engineering, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence\u00a0- Social and economic sciences (e.g., Business Administration or Economics)- Psychology, Cognitive Sciences (e.g., Organizational or Business Psychology) Language skills: You are fluent and able to express yourself very well in both spoken and written English. Fluency in German is a big plus but not mandatory Motivation: Strong motivation to contribute to the interdisciplinary agenda of the Institute. Highly motivated, curious, well organized, team player Software engineering and data science: You have experience in at least one of the following areas and are looking forward to developing more expertise in the others: - Data science and statistics (including R or Python) - Software engineering (e.g., Java, Python) - AI pipeline development and maintenance (e.g., in Azure or Kubernetes) - AI use case development, implementation and testing (e.g., Azure or Kubernetes) Additional skills: Experience and intermediate to very good skills in at least one of the following areas are an advantage: - Teaching (e.g., prior experience in tutorials, workshops) - Experimental research (e.g., behavioral and experimental economics, psychology) Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Do you want to join the Digital Ecosystems team? Then please submit your application including Curriculum Vitae Motivation Letter Transcript of your Bachelor and Master studies If applicable: certificate(s) or references for additional skills What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 21, 2026 (ID 2919). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2921.html": {"title": "Research and Teaching Associate", "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institut f\u00fcr Interactive Marketing and Social Media Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting as soon as possible, and ending after 6 years Do you want to find out how advertising, platforms, creators, and public policy shape what consumers buy? The position combines causal inference with large-scale real-world data and AI-based measurement, alongside teaching and work on ongoing research projects. The Institute for Interactive Marketing & Social Media (IMSM) aims to be a leading institution for research and education in digital marketing. Our goal is to produce credible evidence that helps firms, platforms, and policymakers make better decisions and achieve better outcomes for businesses and consumers. We particularly focus on markets where digital advertising, online platforms, creator content, and AI are reshaping how consumers form brand perceptions and make purchases, and where regulators increasingly intervene. Our approach applies causal inference and machine learning, including large language models (LLMs), to large-scale observational and experimental data. What to expect Writing a dissertation: You will develop and pursue your own research agenda at the intersection of digital marketing, platform economics, and empirical marketing research. Your research will be empirical and quantitative, with a strong emphasis on credible causal identification. Current research areas include: Platforms, regulation, and policy: How trade policy, digital advertising taxes, and platform rules affect sellers, advertisers, and consumers in online markets. Creator content and e-commerce: How social media content, such as TikTok videos comparing original products with lower-priced \"dupes,\" affects brand sales and consumer choice. Digital advertising effectiveness and delivery: How targeting choices and platform delivery algorithms shape who sees ads and what ads achieve, studied with large-scale geo-experiments and field experiments. Brands, reputation, and media coverage: How scandals and publicity shape brand perceptions, separating what firms did from how loudly it was covered. Causal inference and AI-based measurement: Combining different econometric approaches (e.g. difference-in-differences, event-study etc.) and experimental designs with machine learning and large language models (e.g., to measure marketing constructs from text, images, and video). Data & infrastructure: You will work with large, proprietary, real-world datasets (e.g., from online platforms, marketplaces, advertisers, and brand-tracking providers) and modern tools for large-scale data processing. Responsible use of AI: You will use AI tools in coding, data processing, and measurement, and help develop good practice for validating and documenting AI-assisted work in our research and teaching. Conferences & network: You will present your work at leading international conferences and collaborate within our international academic network. Teaching & co-supervision: The regular teaching load is approx. one course per term; you will also co-supervise bachelor's and master's theses. Organizational tasks: As part of the team, you will support selected organizational tasks of the institute. What you have to offer You hold a diploma or master's degree with strong academic performance in business, economics, marketing, computer science, data science, statistics, or a related quantitative field that qualifies you for enrollment in a PhD program at WU. You have a strong quantitative mindset and genuine enthusiasm for empirical research \u2013 you enjoy working with large-scale, real-world data and turning it into credible causal evidence. You are proficient in at least one statistical programming language (e.g., Python or R) and eager to deepen your technical skills as part of your PhD training. You are interested in the methods we use across the full research pipeline \u2013 automated data collection (e.g., web scraping, APIs), large-scale data processing (e.g., SQL databases), machine learning and large language models (e.g., embeddings, LLM-based annotation of text, images, or video), and causal inference (e.g., difference-in-differences, event studies, geo- and field experiments, double/debiased ML). You bring AI literacy and a critical, reflective approach to AI tools \u2013 you use generative AI productively, understand its limitations, and verify, validate, and transparently document AI-assisted work. You bring experience in or curiosity about our substantive research domains , such as digital advertising and targeting, platform algorithms, creator content and e-commerce, brand reputation, or the economics and regulation of online markets. You have an excellent command of written and spoken English ; German language skills are an asset. Since the position includes teaching responsibilities, prior teaching or instructional-support experience (e.g., tutoring, grading, course assistance) is appreciated. You are prepared to use multimedia and digital teaching and learning formats and to help students use AI tools critically and responsibly. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2921). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2927.html": {"title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-10-28 Do you want to understand how language and culture are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Intercultural Communication Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting December 01, 2026, and ending after 6 years We explore how culture shapes human interaction and discourse, especially in organizational communication. Our current projects investigate intercultural / multilingual face-to-face and video-mediated interactions (multimodal conversation analysis) and language, culture, and communication in the context of migration. Our teaching focuses on intercultural communication, including cross-cultural competence training courses, applied research projects on migration and diversity, intercultural simulations, as well as general courses on intercultural business communication. What to expect Research: You will contribute to ongoing research projects on language-in-interaction and on organizational decision-making and develop and conduct your independent research projects in the field of intercultural communication (e.g., research on migrants). Teaching: You will teach your own courses and contribute to the development of courses and course materials in intercultural (business) communication, methods courses and applied research projects at bachelor\u2019s and master\u2019s levels. Thesis Supervision: You will give students feedback and help them develop their work, including supervising master\u2019s theses and bachelor\u2019s theses. Organizational and Administrative Tasks: You will share in the institute\u2019s administrative responsibilities, including the organization of international and internal research workshops on topics of mutual interest, and help prepare applications for collaborative grants. You will also contribute at the departmental level (e.g. by reviewing applications for the master\u2019s program). Collaborative Teamwork: You will support tasks related to research, teaching, research-to-practice activities, and collaborate with our researchers on projects, proposals and papers. What you have to offer Academic Background: You have a PhD degree (or equivalent) in a field related to intercultural communication such as linguistics or education, enabling you to design interventions and trainings that facilitate collaboration. Strong academic record: You have an outstanding academic background and qualifications in qualitative research methods, in particular conversation analysis, interview-based research, and observation. Your work clearly relates to intercultural communication and adaptation strategies in complex contexts such as migration. On the level of methodology, it is a plus if you have experience in systematically collecting data and managing access to the field, especially within organizations (e.g., through in-depth interviews or participant observation). Research-to-practice activities: You have contributed with your research to organizations where intercultural communication plays an important role. Passion for academic work: You have a strong dedication to publish your research in top-tier academic journals, and to develop research projects and write funding proposals with our team. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods: You are prepared/ready to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Soft skills: You communicate and present ideas very effectively, work independently and with a high degree of self-motivation, organize tasks efficiently, take responsibility, approach new topics with curiosity, and work well as part of a team. Language skills: You have expert command in written and spoken English. Knowledge of other languages is a plus, in particular as and when relevant for your research in intercultural communication. Willingness to learn German is an advantage. Interest in teaching: You have a proven track record of teaching intercultural (business) communication and qualitative research methods. You are interested in developing research-to-practice formats. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,014.30 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2927). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2930.html": {"title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-11 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Political Economy of Public Policy Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting February 01, 2027, and ending after 6 years Postdoctoral Researcher in Quantitative Social Science Methodology with a strong focus on Political Economy or Comparative Public Policy The Department of Socioeconomics at WU Vienna University of Economics and Business invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track postdoctoral position. We seek a researcher who combines an equally ambitious research agenda in political economy or comparative public policy and in modern quantitative research designs. The position offers the opportunity to pursue theoretically informed, empirically rigorous research in an active and internationally oriented social science environment. We welcome applicants who ask consequential questions about politics, institutions, and socioeconomic change\u2014and bring compelling research designs to bear on them. Substantive interests are open within political economy and comparative public policy. Your research and contribution You will develop an independent research agenda, produce work aimed at leading international journals, and contribute actively to the department\u2019s intellectual life through research exchange and collaboration. We are particularly interested in candidates whose work demonstrates a thoughtful connection between substantive questions, theoretical arguments, and empirical identification. Relevant approaches include experimental and quasi-experimental designs, survey experiments, and advanced observational methods. We value careful measurement, transparent and reproducible research practices, and sound judgment about what the evidence can and cannot establish. Teaching in social science methodology is a central part of the position. You will contribute to the department\u2019s quantitative methods teaching, helping students develop the skills to formulate research questions, assess research designs, and conduct rigorous empirical analyses. There may also be opportunities to teach substantive courses in your area of expertise. Teaching is predominantly in English. An interest in developing externally funded research projects and strengthening international research connections is welcome. Knowledge of German is an asset. How to apply Please apply through WU\u2019s online recruitment system, using position ID 2930. Your application should include: A cover letter outlining your research agenda, methodological expertise, and fit with the position. A curriculum vitae, including your publications. A list of courses taught. Please complete the WU application form. Do not include research papers or references at this stage. We look forward to learning about your research and the contribution you would make to our department. What to expect Conducting independent research: You will actively contribute to the research at the Department of Socioeconomics, publish in top journals in the field, and present at international academic conferences. Teaching and supporting courses: You will plan and teach courses (4 semester hours per week/2 courses each semester) in the Bachelor and Master programs of the Department of Socioeconomics. Supervising students: You will be available to answer students\u2019 questions and act as a supervisor for bachelor\u2019s and master\u2019s theses. Benefiting from a strong researcher environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own research projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. Organizational tasks: As part of the team, you will support selected organizational tasks of the department and/or the institute. Building up a professional network: You will be using the post-doc phase to establish yourself as an independent researcher and expand your own professional network, keeping the WU\u2019s third mission and societal engagement in mind. What you have to offer Your profile We are looking for applicants with: Academic degree: A PhD or equivalent qualification in political science or a closely related discipline. Research Profile: A distinctive research agenda in political economy or comparative public policy, with the potential to make significant contributions to international scholarship. Methodological Expertise: A research agenda in quantitative social science methodology. Research Excellence: Evidence of research excellence appropriate to career stage, demonstrated through publications and a pipeline of research aimed at leading social science journals. Teaching experience: Expertise in advanced quantitative methods and an experience in teaching research methods. Teaching Excellence: A commitment to excellent teaching and the ability to explain demanding methodological concepts clearly, ideally supported by experience teaching quantitative social science methods. Teamwork: A collaborative approach and a willingness to participate actively in the department\u2019s research and teaching community. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2930). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistant-Professor-non-tenure-track-eng-j2931.html": {"title": "Assistant Professor, non-tenure track", "description": "Job opportunity Assistant Professor, non-tenure track at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Assistant Professor, non-tenure track Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Fulltime published till: 2026-11-04 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Political Economy of Public Policy Fulltime, 40 hours/week Starting February 01, 2027, or soon thereafter, and limited for 6 years The Department of Socioeconomics at the WU Vienna University of Economics and Business invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Assistant Professor position (post-doc). The Department of Socioeconomics offers an active and internationally oriented research environment with a focus on interdisciplinary approaches to understanding and addressing today\u2019s major economic, social, and ecological challenges. The position is located in the Institute for Political Economy of Public Policy, and the successful candidate will work in the research group of Prof. Florian Keusch. The successful candidate is expected to complement and strengthen the department\u2019s existing research profile through combining advanced computational methods with research questions and theories grounded in the social sciences. We value careful measurement, transparent and reproducible research practices, and sound judgment about what the evidence can and cannot establish. In addition to independent research, the successful candidate will also contribute to the department\u2019s quantitative methodological teaching portfolio and take over responsibility for administrative and organizational tasks. What to expect Conducting independent research: You will actively contribute to the research at the research group, publish in top journals in the field, and present at international academic conferences. Teaching and supporting courses: You will plan and teach courses (4 semester hours per week/2 courses each semester) in the Bachelor and Master programs of the Department Socioeconomics. Supervising students: You will be available to answer students\u2019 questions and act as a supervisor for bachelor\u2019s and master\u2019s theses. Benefiting from a strong researcher environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own research projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. Working as part of a team: You will join a team of committed researchers who collaboratively advance research projects, including joint funding applications and acquisition of third party-funds. Organizational tasks: As part of the team, you will support selected organizational tasks at the research group. Building up a professional network: You will be using the post-doc phase to establish yourself as an independent researcher and expand your own professional network, keeping the WU\u2019s third mission and societal engagement in mind. What you have to offer Doctoral degree/PhD: You have successfully completed your doctoral degree (PhD or equivalent) in sociology, political science, economics, statistics, or computational social science/social data science (or a closely related field). Subject-specific competences: You conduct research in the field of social data science by applying state-of-the-art computational, quantitative methods to solve real-world social problems with data. Apart from an applied research focus in the core social sciences, your research also advances social science methods (e.g., acquiring and integrating non-traditional data sources, applying NLP, AI, and other emerging technologies to social science research). Methodological skills: You have expertise in advanced quantitative methods and are proficient in the use of statistical programming languages (e.g., R or Python). High-quality research output: You have publications in leading peer-reviewed social science journals appropriate to career stage and have presented your work internationally. Research funding: You are interested in developing externally funded research projects and strengthening international research connections. Teaching experience: You are committed to excellent teaching and the ability to explain demanding methodological concepts clearly, ideally supported by experience teaching quantitative social science methods. You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Language skills: You have an excellent command of written and spoken English. Knowledge of German is an asset. Team spirit: You can demonstrate flexibility, commitment, creativity, and engagement, and are willing to work in a collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. Please submit the following materials as a single PDF file , in this order: Cover letter including earliest possible and preferred start date Academic CV Contact details for at least two academic references (name, affiliation, email address) \u2013 references will be contacted for shortlisted candidates Personal statement (briefly outlining research, teaching, and service activities; max 2 pages) Teaching evaluations (if available) One writing sample, ideally solo- or first-authored journal publication, conference paper, or working paper Transcript of grade records Copies of relevant certificates Application documents must be submitted in English through the WU online application tool (Reference number: [ID 2931]). For questions about the position, please contact Prof. Florian Keusch at florian.keusch@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits . The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac5,079.50 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on equivalent prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 04, 2026 (ID 2931). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistenzprofessorin-Tenure-Track-Qualifizierungsvereinbar-de-j2925.html": {"title": "Assistenzprofessor*in Tenure Track (Qualifizierungsvereinbarung)", "description": "Stellenangebot Assistenzprofessor*in Tenure Track (Qualifizierungsvereinbarung) bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zur\u00fcck Jetzt bewerben! Assistenzprofessor*in Tenure Track (Qualifizierungsvereinbarung) Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4t Wien Forschung, Entwicklung, Lehre Vollzeit Publizierung bis: 04.11.2026 Sie m\u00f6chten Zusammenh\u00e4nge verstehen und Grundlegendes bewegen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten k\u00f6nnen. An einer der gr\u00f6\u00dften und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4ten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualit\u00e4t auch Lebensqualit\u00e4t ist. Wir suchen Verst\u00e4rkung in der Abteilung f\u00fcr Unternehmensrecht I Vollzeit, 40 Stunden/Woche Ab 01.09.2027 befristet f\u00fcr die Dauer von 6 Jahren Eine Qualifizierungsvereinbarung wird bei Beginn des Arbeitsverh\u00e4ltnisses abgeschlossen (\u00a7 27 KollV). Der WU Personalentwicklungsplan sieht f\u00fcr diese Stelle eine maximale Befristung von 6 Jahren vor. Sind alle vereinbarten Ziele erf\u00fcllt, kann das Arbeitsverh\u00e4ltnis in ein unbefristetes \u00fcbergehen. Mitarbeitende, die eine Qualifizierungsvereinbarung erfolgreich abgeschlossen haben, werden als assoziierte Professor*innen eingestuft und geh\u00f6ren organisationsrechtlich zur Gruppe der Professor*innen. Drei Jahre nach erfolgreichem Abschluss der Qualifizierungsvereinbarung sind sie gem\u00e4\u00df \u00a7 43a WU-Satzung berechtigt, die Bestellung zum/zur Full Professor zu beantragen. Das Institut f\u00fcr Unternehmensrecht forscht und lehrt im Bereich des Unternehmensrechts und bereitet die Studierenden auf ihre sp\u00e4tere T\u00e4tigkeit in der Wirtschaft, Beratung, \u00f6ffentlichen Verwaltung oder Wissenschaft vor. Diese Stelle gibt die M\u00f6glichkeit des Weges in die Wissenschaft. Was Sie erwartet Die ausgeschriebene Stelle liegt im Bereich des Unternehmensrechts, insbesondere im Bereich des Stiftungsrechts und der Rechtsvergleichung und einem weiteren Fach (Gesellschaftsrecht, Stiftungsrecht, Rechtsvergleichung). Ein Schwerpunkt der Stelle liegt auf der Mitwirkung im Lehrprogramm des Instituts; der zweite Schwerpunkt im Beitrag zur nachhaltigen Sicherung der Stellung des Instituts als f\u00fchrende und national und international sichtbare Forschungseinrichtung durch den Aufbau eines eigenst\u00e4ndigen Forschungsprofils im Stiftungsrecht und Unternehmens-Governance. Was Sie mitbringen Ihr Profil: Sie haben ein rechtswissenschaftliches Doktoratsstudium abgeschlossen und eine Dissertation mit Schwerpunkt im Unternehmensrecht, Gesellschafts- und Stiftungsrecht oder im Bereich der Rechtsvergleichung verfasst. Wissenschaftliche Qualifikation: Sie haben eine Ihrem akademischen Alter entsprechend hervorragende wissenschaftliche Qualifikation, insbesondere im Unternehmensrecht und/oder Stiftungsrecht und k\u00f6nnen dies durch Publikationen und Vortr\u00e4ge nachweisen. Kenntnisse im Zusammenhang mit dem Stiftungsrecht oder Stiftungswesen sind von Vorteil. Akademische Mobilit\u00e4t: Sie bringen WU-externe System- und Organisationserfahrung mit, da Sie Ihr Doktoratsstudium an einer anderen Universit\u00e4t absolviert haben oder zum Zeitpunkt des geplanten Stellenantritts eine zumindest zweij\u00e4hrige durchg\u00e4ngige Anstellung als post doc mit einer Mindestanstellungszeit von 20 Stunden pro Woche an einer anderen Universit\u00e4t oder renommierten au\u00dferuniversit\u00e4ren Forschungseinrichtung nachweisen k\u00f6nnen. Internationale Erfahrung: Sie haben idealerweise zus\u00e4tzliche internationale Erfahrung durch Forschung und/oder Lehre in mehr als einer Rechtsordnung durch Doktorat im Ausland oder mindestens zweij\u00e4hrige T\u00e4tigkeit an einer ausl\u00e4ndischen Forschungseinrichtung nach dem Doktorat einschlie\u00dflich Lehrt\u00e4tigkeit. Lehre: Sie sind bereit und qualifiziert am Lehrprogramm des Instituts mitzuwirken und dies weiterzuentwickeln. Wissenschaftliche Projekte: Sie sind bereit, wissenschaftliche Projekte selbstst\u00e4ndig zu konzipieren und abzuwickeln sowie Drittmittel einzuwerben und verf\u00fcgen idealerweise bereits \u00fcber entsprechende Erfahrung. Wissenschaftliche Veranstaltungen: Sie sind bereit, wissenschaftliche Veranstaltungen selbstst\u00e4ndig zu konzipieren und abzuwickeln und verf\u00fcgen idealerweise bereits \u00fcber entsprechende Erfahrung. Engagement: Dokumentiertes Interesse an der Mitwirkung in der universit\u00e4ren Selbstverwaltung sowie au\u00dferuniversit\u00e4res Engagement sind erw\u00fcnscht. Sprachen: Sie verf\u00fcgen \u00fcber ausgezeichnete Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift. Multimedia-Lehrbereitschaft: Sie sind bereit, multimediale Lehr- und Lernformate anzuwenden und weiterzuentwickeln. Was wir Ihnen bieten 6 Wochen Urlaub/Erholungszeit Flexible Arbeitszeiten Vielf\u00e4ltiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt \u00fcber Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielf\u00e4ltigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit \u00fcber 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute \u00f6ffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr dar\u00fcber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt betr\u00e4gt 5.980,80 Euro brutto. Dar\u00fcber hinaus bieten wir eine Vielzahl an attraktiven Sozialleistungen an. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis sp\u00e4testens 04.11.2026 (Kennzahl: 2925). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Die WU sch\u00e4tzt Diversit\u00e4t und Inklusion und bem\u00fcht sich aktiv um ein vielf\u00e4ltiges wissenschaftliches Team. Wir laden insbesondere Frauen herzlich zur Bewerbung ein. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterst\u00fctzt. Die Qualifikationen der Bewerber*innen werden im Kontext des jeweiligen akademischen Werdegangs bewertet. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind f\u00fcr die Funktionalit\u00e4t unserer Website erforderlich\nund k\u00f6nnen in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgew\u00e4hlt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen \u00fcber unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. W\u00e4hlen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch k\u00f6nnen Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. W\u00e4hlen Notwendige Cookies Webstatistik"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Assistenzprofessorin-Tenure-Track-Qualifizierungsvereinbar-de-j2926.html": {"title": "Assistenzprofessor*in Tenure Track (Qualifizierungsvereinbarung)", "description": "Stellenangebot Assistenzprofessor*in Tenure Track (Qualifizierungsvereinbarung) bei think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. DEUTSCH ENGLISH Jobangebote Karriere @ WU Wien Zur\u00fcck Jetzt bewerben! Assistenzprofessor*in Tenure Track (Qualifizierungsvereinbarung) Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4t Wien Forschung, Entwicklung, Lehre Vollzeit Publizierung bis: 04.11.2026 Sie m\u00f6chten Zusammenh\u00e4nge verstehen und Grundlegendes bewegen? Bei uns finden Sie das Umfeld, in dem Sie Ihr Potenzial entfalten k\u00f6nnen. An einer der gr\u00f6\u00dften und modernsten Wirtschaftsuniversit\u00e4ten Europas. Auf einem Campus, an dem Arbeitsqualit\u00e4t auch Lebensqualit\u00e4t ist. Wir suchen Verst\u00e4rkung in der Abteilung f\u00fcr Unternehmensrecht I Vollzeit, 40 Stunden/Woche Ab 01.10.2027 befristet f\u00fcr die Dauer von 6 Jahren Eine Qualifizierungsvereinbarung wird bei Beginn des Arbeitsverh\u00e4ltnisses abgeschlossen (\u00a7 27 KollV). Der WU Personalentwicklungsplan sieht f\u00fcr diese Stelle eine maximale Befristung von 6 Jahren vor. Sind alle vereinbarten Ziele erf\u00fcllt, kann das Arbeitsverh\u00e4ltnis in ein unbefristetes \u00fcbergehen. Mitarbeitende, die eine Qualifizierungsvereinbarung erfolgreich abgeschlossen haben, werden als assoziierte Professor*innen eingestuft und geh\u00f6ren organisationsrechtlich zur Gruppe der Professor*innen. Drei Jahre nach erfolgreichem Abschluss der Qualifizierungsvereinbarung sind sie gem\u00e4\u00df \u00a7 43a WU-Satzung berechtigt, die Bestellung zum/zur Full Professor zu beantragen. Das Institut f\u00fcr Unternehmensrecht forscht und lehrt im Bereich des Unternehmensrechts und bereitet die Studierenden auf ihre sp\u00e4tere T\u00e4tigkeit in der Wirtschaft, Beratung, \u00f6ffentlichen Verwaltung oder Wissenschaft vor. Diese Stelle gibt die M\u00f6glichkeit des Weges in die Wissenschaft. Was Sie erwartet Die ausgeschriebene Stelle liegt im Bereich des Unternehmensrechts, insbesondere im Bereich des Gesellschafts- und Kapitalmarkt- und Finanzmarktrechts und der Rechtsvergleichung und einem weiteren Fach (Kapitalmarktrecht, Finanzmarktrecht, Rechtsvergleichung). Ein Schwerpunkt der Stelle liegt auf der Mitwirkung im Lehrprogramm des Instituts; der zweite Schwerpunkt im Beitrag zur nachhaltigen Sicherung der Stellung des Instituts als f\u00fchrende und national und international sichtbare Forschungseinrichtung durch den Aufbau eines eigenst\u00e4ndigen Forschungsprofils. Was Sie mitbringen Ihr Profil: Sie haben ein rechtswissenschaftliches Doktoratsstudium abgeschlossen und eine Dissertation mit Schwerpunkt im Unternehmensrecht, Kapitalmarktrecht oder im Bereich der Rechtsvergleichung verfasst. Wissenschaftliche Qualifikation: Sie haben eine Ihrem akademischen Alter entsprechend hervorragende wissenschaftliche Qualifikation, insbesondere im Unternehmensrecht und/oder Kapitalmarktrecht und k\u00f6nnen dies durch Publikationen und Vortr\u00e4ge nachweisen. Kenntnisse im Zusammenhang mit der Digitalisierung im Unternehmens- oder Kapitalmarktrecht sind von Vorteil. Akademische Mobilit\u00e4t: Sie bringen WU-externe System- und Organisationserfahrung mit, da Sie Ihr Doktoratsstudium an einer anderen Universit\u00e4t absolviert haben oder zum Zeitpunkt des geplanten Stellenantritts eine zumindest zweij\u00e4hrige durchg\u00e4ngige Anstellung als post doc mit einer Mindestanstellungszeit von 20 Stunden pro Woche an einer anderen Universit\u00e4t oder renommierten au\u00dferuniversit\u00e4ren Forschungseinrichtung nachweisen k\u00f6nnen. Internationale Erfahrung: Sie haben idealerweise zus\u00e4tzliche internationale Erfahrung durch Forschung und/oder Lehre in mehr als einer Rechtsordnung durch Doktorat im Ausland oder mindestens zweij\u00e4hrige T\u00e4tigkeit an einer ausl\u00e4ndischen Forschungseinrichtung nach dem Doktorat einschlie\u00dflich Lehrt\u00e4tigkeit. Lehre: Sie sind bereit und qualifiziert am Lehrprogramm des Instituts mitzuwirken und dies weiterzuentwickeln. Wissenschaftliche Projekte: Sie sind bereit, wissenschaftliche Projekte selbstst\u00e4ndig zu konzipieren und abzuwickeln sowie Drittmittel einzuwerben und verf\u00fcgen idealerweise bereits \u00fcber entsprechende Erfahrung. Wissenschaftliche Veranstaltungen: Sie sind bereit, wissenschaftliche Veranstaltungen selbstst\u00e4ndig zu konzipieren und abzuwickeln und verf\u00fcgen idealerweise bereits \u00fcber entsprechende Erfahrung. Engagement: Dokumentiertes Interesse an der Mitwirkung in der universit\u00e4ren Selbstverwaltung sowie au\u00dferuniversit\u00e4res Engagement sind erw\u00fcnscht. Sprachen: Sie verf\u00fcgen \u00fcber ausgezeichnete Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift. Multimedia-Lehrbereitschaft: Sie sind bereit, multimediale Lehr- und Lernformate anzuwenden und weiterzuentwickeln. Was wir Ihnen bieten 6 Wochen Urlaub/Erholungszeit Flexible Arbeitszeiten Vielf\u00e4ltiges Angebot an Weiterbildung Zahlreiche Benefits , von Betriebsarzt \u00fcber Sportangebote und Essenszuschuss bis hin zu vielf\u00e4ltigen Mitarbeitenden-Rabatten Sinnstiftende Arbeit , in einem weltoffenen, inklusiven und familienfreundlichen Arbeitsklima Architektonisch herausragender, moderner Campus mitten in Wien Inspirierendes Campusleben mit \u00fcber 2.400 Mitarbeitenden in Forschung, Lehre und Verwaltung und rund 21.500 Studierenden Sehr gute \u00f6ffentliche Erreichbarkeit Neugierig geworden? Mehr dar\u00fcber was die WU als Arbeitgeberin besonders macht, erfahren Sie unter www.wu.ac.at/benefits Das monatliche Mindestentgelt betr\u00e4gt 5.980,80 Euro brutto. Dar\u00fcber hinaus bieten wir eine Vielzahl an attraktiven Sozialleistungen an. Wollen Sie Teil der WU werden? Dann bewerben Sie sich bitte bis sp\u00e4testens 04.11.2026 (Kennzahl: 2926). Wir freuen uns auf Sie! Die WU sch\u00e4tzt Diversit\u00e4t und Inklusion und bem\u00fcht sich aktiv um ein vielf\u00e4ltiges wissenschaftliches Team. Wir laden insbesondere Frauen herzlich zur Bewerbung ein. Sie sind sich nicht sicher, ob Ihr Profil unseren Anforderungen entspricht? Bewerben Sie sich trotzdem! Frauen werden bei gleicher Qualifikation bevorzugt aufgenommen. Bewerber*innen mit Behinderungen werden in allen Phasen des Bewerbungsprozesses unterst\u00fctzt. Die Qualifikationen der Bewerber*innen werden im Kontext des jeweiligen akademischen Werdegangs bewertet. IMPRESSUM DATENSCHUTZ Einstellungen Cookies Notwendige Cookies Diese Cookies sind f\u00fcr die Funktionalit\u00e4t unserer Website erforderlich\nund k\u00f6nnen in unserem System nicht ausgeschaltet werden. Vorausgew\u00e4hlt Webstatistik Wir verwenden diese Cookies, um statistische Informationen \u00fcber unsere Website\nbereitzustellen. Sie werden zur Leistungsmessung und -verbesserung verwendet. W\u00e4hlen Soziale Netzwerke & Embeds Auf einigen Seiten betten wir Inhalte von Sozialen Netzwerken und anderen Diensten ein. Dadurch k\u00f6nnen Ihre personenbezogenen Daten an den Betreiber des Portals, von dem der Inhalt stammt, weitergegeben werden, so dass dieser Ihr Verhalten analysieren kann. W\u00e4hlen Notwendige Cookies Webstatistik"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Project-staff-member-Teaching-and-Research-Assistant-eng-j2929.html": {"title": "Project staff member (Teaching and Research Assistant)", "description": "Job opportunity Project staff member  (Teaching and Research Assistant) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Project staff member  (Teaching and Research Assistant) Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Sociology and Social Research Part-time, 10 hours/week Starting November 01, 2026, and limited until June 30, 2029 Please note that pursuant to the Collective Bargaining Agreement, only students who have not yet completed a master or diploma degree program can be employed. Qualified candidates with disabilities are especially encouraged to apply for this position. If necessary, a reduction of the extent of employment is possible. Would you like to work in an internationally oriented research environment at the intersection of economic sociology, digital sociology and criminology? As a Research Assistant (10 hours/week) at the Institute for Sociology and Social Research at WU Vienna, you will contribute to the research project A Socio-Technical Framework for Online Drug Markets , led by Dr. Meropi Tzanetakis. The project investigates how illicit drug markets are socially organised and how their organisation is changing through digitalisation. We understand markets not simply as mechanisms of supply and demand, but as socially embedded institutional arrangements in which actors coordinate exchange, establish trust, evaluate goods and manage uncertainty. The project examines how digital infrastructures, organisational arrangements and social practices interact to shape market coordination and governance. Rather than treating digital technologies as external tools that merely facilitate exchange, the research asks how platforms, algorithms, data and other infrastructures become part of the organisation of markets themselves. Empirically, the project examines the changing organisation of illicit drug markets across online, offline and hybrid environments, with attention to their socioeconomic, technological, political, cultural and gendered embeddedness. If you are interested in the social organisation of markets, digital transformation and interdisciplinary research on contemporary economic and societal processes, we look forward to receiving your application. More information about the project and research group: meropitzanetakis.com/research-group.html What to expect Research support: You will contribute to the project\u2019s ongoing research activities, including conducting literature searches, transcribing interviews, collecting, processing and analysing data, and supporting the preparation of academic publications, research reports, and funding applications. You will also present information on research progress and have the opportunity to develop ideas for your Master\u2019s thesis within the thematic scope of the project. Organisational and administrative support: You will assist with organisational and public-relations tasks, contribute to the coordination of project activities, and support the organisation of academic and outreach events. Communication and dissemination: You will help design and implement communication activities related to the research project, contribute to presenting research findings to academic and professional audiences, and support the communication of data and results in accessible and engaging ways. Networking and collaboration: You will collaborate with research group members, project partners and assist in coordinating research activities. Teamwork and participation: You will work closely with colleagues to contribute to joint decisions and the production of high-quality research. Active participation in team meetings, workshops, and other events within the research group and wider academic community will be an integral part of your role. What you have to offer You are currently enrolled in a Master\u2019s program at WU Vienna , preferably in Socioeconomics / SEEP / WUPOL. You hold a bachelor\u2019s degree in a related social science field and are at the beginning of your master\u2019s studies at WU or an advanced bachelor student intending to start a Master\u2019s at WU. You have demonstrated strong academic performance and a keen interest for academic work in curricular as well as extracurricular activities and achievements. You possess very good skills in both German and English (written and spoken) for academic communication. You are familiar with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods , and ideally have prior experience with data analysis tools such as R, Python, Stata, SPSS and/or NVivo, MAXQDA etc. You are flexible, reliable, organised and conscientious , with a strong sense of responsibility for completing assigned research tasks accurately and on time. You have good communication and collaboration skills and enjoy working as part of an interdisciplinary research team. Previous experience in academic research and/or university-level teaching is an advantage. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac689.80. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2929). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Project-staff-member-pre-doc-eng-j2928.html": {"title": "Job opportunity Project staff member (pre-doc)", "description": "Job opportunity Project staff member (pre-doc) at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. In order to provide you with the best possible service and to facilitate the use of certain functions, we use cookies. By using this site, you agree to the use of cookies. For more information about which data is stored, click here. . Allow Customize cookies Decline German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Project staff member (pre-doc) Vienna University of Economics and Business IT Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-11 Do you want to use data to understand why the energy transition is so hard, and how to accelerate it? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential, at one of Europe's largest and most modern business and economics universities, on a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Data, Energy, and Sustainability Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting January 01, 2027, and limited until September 30, 2029 We are hiring a pre-doctoral researcher (project staff, 30 hours/week) at the Institute for Data, Energy, and Sustainability (IDEaS), led by Prof. Kavita Surana and supported by the BMIMI Endowed Professorship for Data-Driven Knowledge Generation: Climate Action. The position starts on January 1, 2027 and ends on September 30, 2029. What to expect You will join a research group that develops data-driven evidence for energy transitions and climate action, starting from the research question and then building the data needed to answer it. This position focuses on (i) why capital-intensive energy technologies and infrastructures, such as offshore wind, geothermal, hydrogen, carbon capture, utilization and storage (CCUS), and energy grids, succeed or stall, and (ii) how technology, firms, investors, and policy shape those outcomes. You will build novel datasets by designing pipelines that combine and harmonize sources, with a special emphasis on turning unstructured and scattered information into structured, validated data using NLP, large language models (LLMs), or other relevant methods. You will then analyze these data with empirical methods, such as econometrics and statistical or network analysis. You will work in a highly interdisciplinary, international environment, with dedicated mentoring and regular, constructive feedback to support your growth as a researcher. As part of the institute's team, your responsibilities will include: Conducting research: You will contribute to the institute's research projects, build and maintain high-quality datasets and data pipelines, and publish in leading international peer-reviewed journals. Writing a dissertation: You will pursue a PhD at WU and devote one third of your working hours to your dissertation, which can complement your project work Supervision: You will co-supervise bachelor's and/or master's theses. Engaging with external stakeholders: You will work with the institute's partners in industry, government, and academia to co-develop and communicate research insights. Supporting organizational duties: You will take on organizational and administrative tasks for the institute. Supporting teaching: Independent teaching within this position is available to support your career path -- non-continuous teaching of max. 3 SWS is supported as part of an external teaching assignment outside working hours. Within working hours, you will support the institute's teaching, including preparing course materials and assisting with the organization and delivery of courses at the bachelor's and/or master's level. What you have to offer Academic degree: You have a master's degree (or equivalent) that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU, in a quantitative or analytical field such as data science, computer science, information systems, statistics, mathematics, physics, economics, or engineering (especially with a focus on empirical or data analysis). An interdisciplinary degree in the social sciences, public policy, or management with substantial quantitative training also qualifies. Essential skills: Building datasets: Demonstrated experience constructing datasets from unstructured or heterogeneous sources, and motivation to build novel datasets rather than only analyze existing ones. Coding: Advanced proficiency in Python or R, including version control, shown through projects, a thesis, or code you can share. Empirical analysis: Training in econometrics or statistics. Interest in energy and climate: Genuine motivation to work on the energy transition, especially on capital-intensive energy technologies and infrastructure. Experience in any of the following is a plus: web scraping and data collection, document and information extraction, data integration and entity resolution, NLP and large language models, knowledge graphs, network science or complex systems, and a background in energy technology innovation, climate tech, energy policy, climate finance, industrial policy, or energy economics. You do not need all of these. We care more about how you approach a data problem than about any specific method. Language skills: You have excellent skills of written and spoken English. Knowledge of German (or willingness to learn it) is a plus. Working style: You take ownership of your work and enjoy being part of a team where people contribute to each other's success. You set high standards for yourself, care as much about asking the right question as about applying the right method, and thrive in an interdisciplinary, collaborative environment where you engage with multiple audiences. Please submit at least the following documents with your application: (a) A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) in which you engage critically with a recent paper (published in the last 3 years) by scholars in our group on the scaling or development of energy technologies or infrastructure. For example, you might discuss a limitation in its data or approach, a question it leaves open, or a dataset that could extend it. Explain the research directions you would like to pursue building on this paper, including the question that interests you and the data sources you would need to develop. (b) A curriculum vitae, including a list of publications (if applicable) and the names and contact details of two references (prior employers or academic supervisors). (c) Transcripts and grades from your master's and bachelor's studies, including your master's or diploma thesis grade. (d) A work sample that demonstrates your data science skills, e.g., a link to a code repository (GitHub or similar), your master's thesis, or a paper. We particularly encourage women to apply, including those from analytical fields who are new to energy or climate topics but have a strong interest in them. Please direct any questions to Prof. Kavita Surana at kavita.surana@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,877.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 11, 2026 (ID 2928). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Cookie settings Close Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies sid Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 1 hour Contains an anonymous user ID so that multiple requests from one user can be assigned to the same HTTP session. cookieconsent_status Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 days This cookie stores your cookie settings for this website. Web statistics _pk_id* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 13 months Registers a unique ID for a website visitor, which logs how the visitor uses the website. The data is used for statistics. _pk_ref* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 6 months This cookie is used as a reference for the anonymous tracking session on the site. _pk_ses* Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: 30 Minuten This cookie stores a unique session ID. MATOMO_SESSID Domain name: jobs.wu.ac.at Expire: This session cookie will be deleted when the browser is closed This cookie stores the website visit based on a session or visitor ID. Save changes Abort"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2924.html": {"title": "Research and Teaching Associate", "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-10-28 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Marketing and Customer Analytics Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting November 01, 2026, and ending after 6 years The Institute for Marketing and Customer Analytics is seeking applications for the position as a Teaching and Research Associate (Universit\u00e4tsassistent*in prae doc; 30 hours per week). The position is ideal for individuals who wish to deepen their quantitative marketing skills and join applied research projects on the interfaces between marketing and data science. It opens doors to an academic career for a self-motivated, team-oriented, highly active and productive researcher, who will be expected to make a significant contribution to the Institute\u2019s research areas. About the Institute: We aim at being a leading institution for research and education in the field of marketing and customer analytics. The marketing landscape is being radically transformed by advances of information technology, online media and artificial intelligence (AI) enabled tools. We recognize these emerging challenges by developing innovative tools that support consumers and managers in making better decisions. Our research is interdisciplinary with links to statistics, economics, psychology, and computer science. We leverage advanced statistical techniques, machine learning and generative AI to develop marketing models for managerial decision support. Our students seek research-driven course content and wish to acquire analytical skills in marketing research, business analytics, and decision support. What to expect Writing a dissertation: You will be investigating your research topic and spending a third of your working hours on writing your dissertation in the rapidly growing field of applying machine learning and AI in marketing. Research for yourself and others: You will support publications, conduct experiments and research projects in co-operation with colleagues from WU\u2019s marketing and customer analytics group and international cooperation partners. Ideally, your set of skills is compatible with the Institute\u2019s current research projects (learn more at: https://www.wu.ac.at/mca/research). Learning from top researchers: You will have the opportunity to work together with renowned researchers in the marketing field and to learn from them. Recurring research and PhD seminars will help you to improve your ongoing research projects. Teaching courses and teaching support: You will be planning and teaching courses in the field of marketing and customer analytics at the Bachelor\u2019s level independently and co-teach at the MSc level. Student support: You will be available to answer students\u2019 questions, provide feedback on seminar papers, coach students in their projects and act as a co-advisor for bachelor and master theses. Teamwork: You will be working to advance research in the area of marketing and customer analytics together with an experienced and truly international team. Look forward to a welcoming atmosphere and open-minded discussions. Building and enhancing your personal network: You will create or enhance your own professional network for the future. What you have to offer Academic degree: We are looking for applicants with a solid academic qualification, i.e., an outstanding master\u2019s degree (or equivalent qualification) in economics, marketing analytics, information systems, business engineering, mathematics, physics, statistics, or computer science (or a related field) with a strong focus on quantitative topics -- such as marketing science, econometrics, operations research, machine learning, or finance -- that qualifies you for enrollment in a doctoral program at WU. Data analytical skills: You have outstanding prior knowledge of statistics and empirical research methods. This includes analyzing data using statistical models and econometric techniques (e.g., using R, Matlab or Python) and/or machine learning skills (e.g., using PyTorch). Experience in marketing and customer analytics: Experience in the field of marketing analytics and customer research (e.g., through internships, student jobs, or working on one\u2019s own website) is beneficial. Communication skills: For research and teaching purposes, we expect you to have an excellent oral and written command of English, ideally also proficiency in German. Ability to develop and deliver excellent teaching at Bachelor\u2019s and/or Master\u2019s level in marketing marketing-related fields. Any prior teaching and/or publishing experience would be ideal but is not essential. Willingness to use multimedia teaching methods : You are prepared to use multimedia teaching and learning formats. Working style: We look for enthusiastic, curious team players, who are passionate about marketing and customer analytics and research. You work independently, show initiative, are willing to take on responsibility, and have good self-organization skills. What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits Learn more about the Institute\u2019s current research projects at https://www.wu.ac.at/mca/research The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,832.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by October 28, 2026 (ID 2924). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Research-and-Teaching-Associate-eng-j2932.html": {"title": "Research and Teaching Associate", "description": "Job opportunity Research and Teaching Associate at think:impact - Dabei sein, wenn Denken zur Zukunft wird. An der WU Wirtschaftuniversit\u00e4t Wien finden Sie Jobs, um Ihr Potenzial zu entfalten. German English Job offers Careers @ WU Vienna Back Apply now! Research and Teaching Associate Vienna University of Economics and Business Research, development, teaching Part time published till: 2026-11-04 You want to understand how things are connected and make a fundamental impact? We offer an environment where you can realize your full potential. At one of Europe\u2019s largest and most modern business and economics universities. On a campus where quality of work is also quality of life. We are looking for support at the Institute for Political Economy of Public Policy Part-time, 30 hours/week Starting February 01, 2027, or soon thereafter, and limited for 6 years The Department of Socioeconomics at the WU Vienna University of Economics and Business invites applications for a Research and Teaching Associate position (pre-doc). The Department of Socioeconomics offers an active and internationally oriented research environment with a focus on interdisciplinary approaches to understanding and addressing today\u2019s major economic, social, and ecological challenges. The position is located in the Institute for Political Economy of Public Policy, and the successful candidate will work in the research group of Prof. Florian Keusch. The successful candidate is expected to write their dissertation and conduct methodological research at the intersection of survey methodology and social data science (e.g., integrating collection of non-traditional data sources such as digital trace data and sensor data into surveys; applying AI in survey and public opinion research; analytically combining different data sources). In addition to research, the successful candidate will also contribute to the department\u2019s quantitative methodological teaching portfolio and take over responsibility for administrative and organizational tasks. What to expect Conducting research: You plan and carry out high-quality research at the intersection of survey methodology and social data science. Your research will form the basis of presentations at international academic conferences and manuscripts for submission to top journals in the field. Completing doctoral training: You will enroll in WU\u2019s doctoral program and complete doctoral courses as part of your academic training. Writing your dissertation: One third of your working time will be dedicated to writing your doctoral dissertation. Teaching and supporting courses: Starting in the second year, you will plan and (co-)teach courses (2 semester hours per week/1 courses each semester) in the Bachelor programs of the Department Socioeconomics. Supervising students: You will be available to answer students\u2019 questions and act as a co-supervisor for bachelor\u2019s theses. Benefiting from a strong researcher environment: You will work in an excellent, internationally connected team that supports you in developing your own research projects, advancing publications, and expanding your network. Working as part of a team: You will join a team of committed researchers who collaboratively advance research projects. Organizational tasks: As part of the team, you will support selected organizational tasks at the research group. What you have to offer Academic degree: You have a Master\u2019s degree (or equivalent) in sociology, political science, economics, statistics, or computational social science/social data science (or a closely related field) that qualifies you for admission to a doctoral program at WU. Subject-specific competences: You have a strong quantitative mindset and genuine enthusiasm for methodological research questions. You are particularly interested in new ways of collecting social data. Methodological skills: You have experience in quantitative empirical research, are proficient in at least one statistical programming language (e.g., R or Python), and are eager to deepen your methodological and technical skills as part of your doctoral training. Ideally, you have first experience with conducting surveys and/or collecting other types of social data (e.g., digital traces, sensor data, text data). Interest in teaching: You are highly motivated to develop your teaching skills and have the potential to excel in teaching. You are willing to use multimedia and digital teaching and learning formats. Prior teaching or instructional-support experience (e.g., tutoring, grading, course assistance) is appreciated. Language skills: You have an excellent command of written and spoken English. Knowledge of German is an asset. Team spirit: You demonstrate flexibility, commitment, creativity, and engagement, and are willing to work in a collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. Please submit the following materials as a single PDF file, in this order: Cover letter outlining your motivation for an academic career, research interests, and the earliest possible and preferred start date (max 2 pages) Academic CV Contact details for at least one academic reference (name, affiliation, email address) \u2013 references will be contacted for shortlisted candidates One writing sample, e.g., MA thesis or other research-oriented output Transcript of grade records Copies of relevant certificates Application documents must be submitted in English through the WU online application tool (Reference number: [ID 2932]). For questions about the position, please contact Prof. Florian Keusch at florian.keusch@wu.ac.at . What we offer you Six weeks of vacation/Extra vacation time Flexible working hours Training opportunities A wide range of benefits , from an in-house medical officer to athletic activities and a meal allowance to a variety of employee discounts Meaningful work in an open-minded, inclusive, and family-friendly environment A modern campus with spectacular architecture in the heart of Vienna Inspiring campus life with over 2,400 employees in research, teaching, and administration and approximately 21,500 students Excellent accessibility by public transportation Curious? Visit our website and find out more at www.wu.ac.at/benefits The minimum monthly gross salary amounts to \u20ac2,877.08 (14 times per year). This salary may be adjusted based on job-related prior work experience. In addition, we offer a wide range of attractive social benefits. Do you want to join the WU team? Then please submit your application by November 04, 2026 (ID 2932). We are looking forward to hearing from you! WU is committed to diversity and inclusion and actively encourages applications from people of all backgrounds. We particularly welcome applications from women. Not sure if your profile fully matches our requirements? Apply anyway! In case of equal qualification, female candidates will be given preference. Applicants with disabilities will be supported throughout each stage of the recruitment process. Candidates' qualifications will be assessed in the context of their academic age. Imprint Data protection Settings Cookies Necessary cookies These cookies are necessary for a good functionality of our website\nand cannot be switched off in our system. Preselected Web statistics We use these cookies to provide statistical information about our website.\nThey are used to measure and improve performance. Select Social Networks & Embeds On some pages we embed content from social networks and other services. As a result, your personal data may be passed on to the operator of the portal from which the content originates, so that the operator can analyse your behaviour. Select Necessary cookies Web statistics"}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Alternative-position-2-project-staff-members-pre-doc-or-1--eng-j2881.html": {"school_id": 1660, "posting_url": "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Alternative-position-2-project-staff-members-pre-doc-or-1--eng-j2881.html", "job_title_in_post": "Alternative position: 2 project staff members pre-doc or 1 project staff member post doc", "position_type": "Research_Fellow", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Institute for Organization Design", "area_key_words": "Strategic Leadership; Corporate Governance; Full", "deadline_of_application": "September 16, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Full-Professor-of-Strategic-Management-eng-j2821.html": {"school_id": 1660, "posting_url": "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Full-Professor-of-Strategic-Management-eng-j2821.html", "job_title_in_post": "Full Professor of Strategic Management", "position_type": "Full_Professor", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Strategy and Innovation", "area_key_words": "Strategic Management", "deadline_of_application": "November 3, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Systemmanagerin-AV-Medientechnik-de-j2882.html": {"school_id": 1660, "posting_url": "https://jobs.wu.ac.at/Systemmanagerin-AV-Medientechnik-de-j2882.html", "job_title_in_post": "Systemmanager*in AV-Medientechnik", "position_type"